---
title: Feature Extraction
mode: CQP
---

# Feature Extraction

## Initialization

Load helper macros and run `/init[...]`, which takes in one argument (the name of an s-
attribute) to define the subcorpus to query. The corresponding value for this s-attribute
is output alongside each span/hit count.

The macro creates a Named Query Result (NQR) with the name `Corpus`,
which should be re-activated after using a subquery.

```cqp
define macro < "macros/featex.m";
define macro < "macros/mwus.m";
/init_corpus[text_id];
```

The `/union[...]` and `/diff[...]` macros create a set union or difference of the provided
NQRs and save the result in the name of the first argument.

The `/feature[...]` and `feature_count[...]` macros take in a NQR and output a header with its name,
followed by a table of spans/hit counts for the s-attribute specified in `/init[...]`.

## Basic Counts

### Sentences

**Query**: s-attribute `s` (given by markup).

```cqp
Sentences = [] expand to s;
/feature_count[Sentences];
```

### Actual Words

**Query**: alphanumeric part-of-speech tags (excludes punctation).

```cqp
Words = [pos="\w+"];
/feature_count[Words];
```

### Content Words

**Query**: all nouns (N), verbs (V), adjectives (J), and adverbs (R).

TODO: exclude auxiliaries

```cqp
ContentWords = [pos="[NJVR].+" & pos!="RP|VMK?"];
/feature_count[ContentWords];
```

### Noun-based features

#### Common Nouns

```cqp
CommonNouns = [pos="NN[ABLOTU]?[12]?|ND1"];
/feature_count[CommonNouns];
```

#### Proper Nouns

```cqp
ProperNouns = [pos="NP[DM]?[12]"];
/feature_count[ProperNouns];
```

#### Nominalizations

**Definition**: nouns created from adjectives or verbs through *derivation*.
**Query**: a positive wordlist of common nominalizing suffixes in combination with a negative wordlist to exclude certain high frequency false positives.

```cqp
define $NotNominalizedWords < "wordlists/nouns/NotNominalizedWords.txt";
define $NominalizingSuffixes < "wordlists/nouns/NominalizingSuffixes.txt";
Nominalizations = [pos="NN.+" & word=RE($NominalizingSuffixes)%c & word!=RE($NotNominalizedWords)%c];
/feature[Nominalizations];
```

#### Neoclassical Compounds

**Definition**: words composed of affixes and stems from classical Latin or ancient Greek.
**Query**: a positive wordlist of common neoclassical affixes in combination with a negative wordlist to exclude certain high frequency false positives.

```cqp
define $NotNeoclassicalWords < "wordlists/nouns/NotNeoclassicalWords.txt";
define $NeoclassicalAffixes < "wordlists/nouns/NeoclassicalAffixes.txt";
NeoclassicalCompounds = [pos!="NP" & word=RE($NeoclassicalAffixes)%c & word!=RE($NotNeoclassicalWords)%c];
/feature[NeoclassicalCompounds];
```

### Pronouns

```cqp
AllPronouns = [pos="A?P.+"];
/feature_count[AllPronouns];
```

#### Personal Pronouns

TODO: differentiate subjective and objective *you*/*it*

```cqp
# special case for lowercase `I`, which CLAWS consistently mistakes for ZZ1 and MC1
PronounI = [(pos="PPIS1" & word="I"%c) | word="I"%c];
PronounWe = [pos="PPIS2" & word="we"%c];

/feature_count[PronounI];
/feature_count[PronounWe];

PronounMe = [pos="PPIO1" & word="me"%c];
PronounUs = [pos="PPIO2" & word="us"%c];

/feature_count[PronounMe];
/feature_count[PronounUs];

PronounYou = [pos="PPY"];
/feature_count[PronounYou];

PronounHe = [pos="PPHS1" & word="he"%c];
PronounShe = [pos="PPHS1" & word="she"%c];
PronounIt = [word="it"%c];
PronounThey = [pos="PPHS2"];

/feature_count[PronounHe];
/feature_count[PronounShe];
/feature_count[PronounIt];
/feature_count[PronounThey];

PronounHim = [pos="PPHO1" & word="him"%c];
PronounHer = [pos="PPHO1" & word="her"%c];
PronounThem = [pos="PPHO2"];

/feature_count[PronounHim];
/feature_count[PronounHer];
/feature_count[PronounThem];

PronounIndefiniteNeutral = [pos="PN(\d1)?"];
/feature_count[PronounIndefiniteNeutral];

PronounIndefiniteSingular = [pos="PN1"];
/feature_count[PronounIndefiniteSingular];
```

#### Possessive Pronouns

TODO: *its* is never tagged as PPGE

```cqp
PronounMine = [pos="PPGE" & word="mine"%c];
PronounOurs = [pos="PPGE" & word="ours"%c];

/feature_count[PronounMine];
/feature_count[PronounOurs];

PronounYours = [pos="PPGE" & word="yours"%c];

/feature_count[PronounYours];

PronounHis = [pos="PPGE" & word="his"%c];
PronounHers = [pos="PPGE" & word="hers"%c];
PronounIts = [pos="PPGE" & word="its"%c];
PronounTheirs = [pos="PPGE" & word="theirs"%c];

/feature_count[PronounHis];
/feature_count[PronounHers];
/feature_count[PronounIts];
/feature_count[PronounTheirs];
```

#### Reflexive Pronouns

```cqp
PronounMyself = [pos="PPX1" & word="myself"%c];
PronounOurselves = [pos="PPX2" & word="ourselves"%c];

/feature_count[PronounMyself];
/feature_count[PronounOurselves];

PronounYourself = [pos="PPX1" & word="yourself"%c];
PronounYourselves = [pos="PPX2" & word="yourselves"%c];

/feature_count[PronounYourself];
/feature_count[PronounYourselves];

PronounHimself = [pos="PPX1" & word="himself"%c];
PronounHerself = [pos="PPX1" & word="herself"%c];
PronounItself = [pos="PPX1" & word="itself"%c];
PronounThemselves = [pos="PPX2" & word="themselves"%c];

/feature_count[PronounHimself];
/feature_count[PronounHerself];
/feature_count[PronounItself];
/feature_count[PronounThemselves];

PronounReflexiveIndefinite = [pos="PNX1(\d1)?"];
/feature_count[PronounReflexiveIndefinite];
```

### Determiners

TODO: split these up further?

```cqp
Articles = [pos="AT1?"];
/feature_count[Articles];

WhDeterminers = [pos="DDQ(V|GE)"];
/feature_count[WhDeterminers];

PreDeterminers = [pos="DB2?"];
/feature_count[PreDeterminers];

PostDeterminers = [pos="DA[12RT]"];
/feature_count[PostDeterminers];

PossessiveDeterminers = [pos="APPGE"];
/feature_count[PossessiveDeterminers];

OtherDeterminers = [pos="DD[12]?" & word!="this|these|that|those"%c];
/feature_count[OtherDeterminers];
```

### Demonstratives

**Query**:

1. **Demonstrative Determiners**: *this*, *these*, *that*, or *those* followed by a noun (N) or adjective (J)
2. **Demonstrative Pronouns**: all other instances of *this*, *these*, *that*, and *those*

```cqp
Demonstratives = [pos="DD[12]" & word="this|these|that|those"%c];
DemonstrativeDeterminers = [pos="DD[12]" & word="this|these|that|those"%c] np:[::] :: np -> np.pos = "[NJ].+" within s;
/feature[DemonstrativeDeterminers];

/diff[DemonstrativePronouns, Demonstratives, DemonstrativeDeterminers];
/feature[DemonstrativePronouns];
```

### Adjectives

Cases (Quirk et al. 2010: 418):

1. Attributive: "*useful* information"
2. Postpositive: "something *useful*"
3. Predicative: "This information is *useful*."

```cqp
AllAdjectives = [pos="J.+"];
/feature_count[AllAdjectives];
```

#### Attributive Adjectives

**Definition**: adjectives that "premodify the head of a noun phrase" (Quirk et al. 2010: 417).
**Query**: first extracts all premodifiers of nouns and then finds the adjectives within.

```cqp
AttributiveAdjectives = (?longest)(
    (
        ([word=","] | [word=","]? [pos="CCB?"])?
        [pos="R.+"]* [pos="J.+|MD|N.+"]
    )+
    [pos="N.+"]+
) within s;
AttributiveAdjectives;
AttributiveAdjectives = [pos="J.+|MD"];
/feature[AttributiveAdjectives];
Corpus; # reactivate corpus
```

#### Postpositive Adjectives

**Definition**: adjectives that "immediately follow the noun or pronoun they modify" (Quirk et al. 2010: 418).
**Query**:

1. any compound singular indefinite pronoun (PN1) ending in *-body*, *-one*, or *-thing* or a locative adverb (RL) ending in *-where*, followed by an adjective (J)
e.g., "something *nice*"

1. adjectives ending in *-able* or *-ible* when a noun is modified by a superlative adjecitve, the word *only*, or an ordinal
e.g., "the best use *possible*"

1. adjectives following a noun with a prepositional phrase or *to*-infinitive as complement
e.g., "box *full* of chocolate"

1. *proper* in the sense of "strictly defined"
e.g., "the City of London *proper*"

1. institutionalized expressions (mostly in official designations)
e.g., "president _elect" and "heir *apparent*"

TODO: add other cases listed in Quirk et al. (2010)

```cqp
PostpositiveAdjectives1 = [(word=".+(body|one|thing)"%c & pos="PN1") | (word=".+where" & pos="RL")] [pos="J.+"] within s;
set PostpositiveAdjectives1 match matchend;
PostpositiveAdjectives2 = [word="only" | pos="JJT" | pos="MD"] [pos="N.+"] [word=".+[ai]ble" & pos="J.+"] within s;
set PostpositiveAdjectives2 match matchend;
PostpositiveAdjectives3 = [pos="N.+"] [pos="R.+"]* @[pos="J.+"] [pos="I[FIOW]" | pos="TO"] within s;
set PostpositiveAdjectives3 match target;
PostpositiveAdjectives4 = [pos="N.+"] [word="proper"%c] within s;
set PostpositiveAdjectives4 match matchend;
PostpositiveAdjectives5 = "president"%c "elect"%c | "heir"%c "apparent"%c;
set PostpositiveAdjectives5 match matchend;

/union[
    PostpositiveAdjectives,
    PostpositiveAdjectives1,
    PostpositiveAdjectives2,
    PostpositiveAdjectives3,
    PostpositiveAdjectives4,
    PostpositiveAdjectives5
];
/feature[PostpositiveAdjectives];
```

#### Predicative Adjectives

**Definition**: adjectives that "function as subject complement or object complement" (Quirk et al. 2010: 417).
**Query**: negative query (all adjectives that are not attributive or postpositive).

```cqp
/diff[PredicativeAdjectives, AllAdjectives, AttributiveAdjectives, PostpositiveAdjectives];
/feature[PredicativeAdjectives];
```

### Prepositions

**Query**: based on part-of-speech

```cqp
Prepositions = [pos="I.+"];
/feature_count[Prepositions];
```

### Verbs

TODO: extract verb phrases and then check for features below?

```cqp
AllVerbs = [pos="V.+"];
/feature_count[AllVerbs];
```

#### Finite Verbs

**Definition**: verbs that express either tense or modality.
**Query**: based on part-of-speech

For normalization of other verb features.

```cqp
FiniteVerbs = [pos="V.[^ING].?"];
/feature[FiniteVerbs];
```

#### Past Verbs

**Query**: past tense verbs plus *used to*

- also counts *used to* not tagged as a modal when preceded by a noun or pronoun
- includes *I* explicitly because CLAWS tags it incorrectly when not capitalized

```cqp
PastVerbs = [pos="V.D.?" | (pos="VMK" & word="used"%c)] | [pos="[NP].+" | word="I"%c] "used"%c "to"%c within s;
/feature[PastVerbs];
```

#### Future Constructions

**Query**:

- will: a form of *will* as a verb followed by an infinitive with optional negation and adverbs in-between
- going-to:
    1. a form of *be* followed by optional negation and adverbs, the phrase *going to*, and an infinitive
    2. the contractions *gonna* and *I'mma* (plus variations) and an infinitive
- about-to: a form of *be* followed by optional negation and adverbs, the phrase *about to*, and an infinitive

TODO: is-to futures? (may be too ambiguous)

```cqp
# use V.+ instead of VM to counteract tagging errors (hopfully unproblematic
# since the combination of tag, surface form, and infinitive should be unambiguous)
WillFutures = TAB [pos="V.+" & word="will|'ll|wo|shall|sha"%c] [pos="XX"]? [pos="RR.*"]* [pos="V.I"] within s;
/feature[WillFutures];

GoingToFutures1 = [pos="VB.+"] [pos="XX"]? [pos="RR.*"]* @[word="going" | pos="VVGK"] [pos="TO"] [pos="V.I"] within s;
GoingToFutures2 = [word="I'?mm?a"%c | word="gonna"%c] [pos="V.I"];
/union[GoingToFutures, GoingToFutures1, GoingToFutures2];
/feature[GoingToFutures];

AboutToFutures = [pos="VB.+"] [pos="XX"]? [pos="RR.*"]* "about"%c [pos="TO"] [pos="V.I"] within s;
/feature[AboutToFutures];
```

### Modal Verbs

**Query**: *can*, *would*, *could*, *should*, *may*, *must*, *might* (plus contractions and excluding will)

TODO: have to, be able to, be allowed to, etc.

```cqp
ModalVerbs = [pos="VM" & word!="will|'ll|wo|shall|sha"%c];
/feature_count[ModalVerbs];
```

## Grammatical Structures

### To-Infinitives

**Query**: the word *to* followed by an infinitive (with optional adverbs in-between).

```cqp
ToInfinitives = [pos="TO" | word="to" %c] [pos="RR.*"]* [pos="V.I"] within s;
set ToInfinitives match matchend;
/feature[ToInfinitives];
```

### Passives

TODO: disambiguate predicative adjectives
TODO: bare (i.e. verbless) passives
TODO: passive interrogatives
TODO: improve nonfinite cases

```cqp
# be + (not + adverbs)? + being? + past participle
# have + (not + adverbs)? + been + being? + past participle
NonModalPassives = (
    [pos="VB[^N].+"] [pos="XX"]? [pos="RR.*"]* |
    [pos="VH.+"] [pos="XX"]? [pos="RR.*"]* [pos="VBN"] [pos="RR.*"]*
) [pos="VBG"]? [pos="V.N.?"] within s;
set NonModalPassives match matchend;

# modal + (not + adverbs)? be (being)? + past participle
# modal + (not + adverbs)? have been (being)? + past participle
ModalPassives = (
    [pos="VM"] [pos="XX"]? [pos="RR.*"]*
    ([pos="VBI"] [pos="RR.*"]* | [pos="VH0"] [pos="RR.*"]* [pos="VBN"])
    [pos="VBG"]? [pos="V.N.?"]
) within s;
set ModalPassives match matchend;

# to + be + past participle
ToPassives = [pos="TO"] [pos="VBI"] [pos="V.N.?"] within s;
set ToPassives match matchend;

# get + past participle
GetPassives = [word="get(s|ting)?|got(ten)?"] ([pos="AT1?"]? [pos="N.+"] | [pos="P.+"])? [pos="RR.*"]* [pos="V.N.?"] within s;
set GetPassives match matchend;

/union[
    Passives,
    NonModalPassives,
    ModalPassives,
    ToPassives,
    GetPassives
];
/feature[Passives];
```

TODO: perfect and progressive aspect

### Coordination and Subordination

```cqp
CoordinatingConjunctions = [pos="CCB?"];
/feature_count[CoordinatingConjunctions];

SubordinatingConjunctions = [pos="CS[ANTW]?"];
/feature_count[SubordinatingConjunctions];
```

### Interrogatives

**Query**:

1. question marks
2. wh-questions
3. yes-no questions
4. tag questions

TODO: clauses before interrogatives?

```cqp
QuestionMarks = "\?" expand to s;
WhQuestions = <s> [pos="CCB?" | word="\p{P}"]? [pos="..Q.*"] [pos="V.*"] within s expand to s;
# AT1 has many false positives
# CLAWS tags many "is that ..." as CST
YNQuestions = <s> [pos="CCB?" | word="\p{P}" & word!="nor"%c]? [pos="V[BDH][^0GIN][RZ]?" | pos="VM"] [pos="XX"]? [pos="PPY" | pos="PP[HI].+" | pos="D[BD]1?" | pos="AT" | pos="NN.?" | pos="APPGE" | pos="CST" | pos="EX"] within s expand to s;
TagQuestions = [pos="V[BDH][^0GIN][RZ]?" | pos="VM"] [pos="XX" & word="n't"] [pos="PPHS[1S][12]?"] </s> within s expand to s;

/union[Interrogatives, QuestionMarks, WhQuestions, YNQuestions, TagQuestions];
/feature[Interrogatives];
```

### Imperatives

**Query**:

1. positive imperatives
e.g., "give me the remote"
2. negative imperatives
e.g., "don't give in"
excludes mental verbs (e.g., know, want) to catch subject ellipses
3. let imperatives
e.g., "let's go to the beach"

TODO: better disambiguation
TODO: more clauses before imperatives
TODO: cases like "Somebody watch my dog."

```cqp
define $MentalWords < "wordlists/process_types/MentalWords.txt";

PositiveImperatives = <s> ([pos="TO"] []+ ",")? [pos="CCB?" | (pos="R.+" & pos!="RRQV?") | word="\p{P}"]? [pos="V.0"] [pos!="V.Z.*|VM.*"] []* [word!="\?"]</s>;
NegativeImperatives = <s> ([pos="TO"] []+ ",")? [pos="CCB?" | word="\p{P}"]? [pos="VD0" & word!=RE($MentalWords)%c] [pos="XX"] [pos="V.I"] [: pos!="RRQ" :] within s expand to s;

# periphrastic first and third person imperatives with let
LetImperatives = [pos="VM21"] [pos="VM22"] [pos="RR.*"]* [pos="V.I.?"] within s expand to s;

/union[Imperatives, PositiveImperatives, NegativeImperatives, LetImperatives];
/feature[Imperatives];
```

### Titles

**Query**:

1. titles following a noun (e.g., M.A.)
2. titles preceding a noun (e.g., Dr.)
3. wordlist to improve recall due to possible tagging errors
4. fixed expressions (at the moment only "the honourable...")

```cqp
NNAs = [pos="NNA"];
NNBs = [pos="NNB"];
define $TitleWords < "wordlists/TitleWords.txt";
TitleWords = @[word=RE($TitleWords)%c] [pos="NP.+"] within s;
set TitleWords matchend target;
Honorables = (?longest) "the"%c "honou?rable"%c [pos="[JN].+"]+ within s;
/union[Titles, NNAs, NNBs, TitleWords, Honorables];
/feature[Titles];
```

### Greetings

#### Salutations

**Query**:

1. casual salutations
2. variations of "good ..."
3. variations of "good ..." with addressee
4. generic addressee singular
5. generic addressee plural
6. royal address
7. variations of "dear ..."

```cqp
CasualSalutations = "hello|hi(ya)?|heya?|yo|sup|whazzup|g'day";

GoodSalutations1 = <s> "good"%c "day|morning|afternoon|evening"%c </s>;
GoodSalutations2 = "good"%c "day|morning|afternoon|evening"%c ("to"%c "you"%c | [pos="N.+"]+) within s;

GenericSalutations1 = TAB "to"%c "whom"%c "it"%c "may"%c "concern"%c within s;
GenericSalutations2 = TAB "lad(y|ies)"%c [pos="CCB?"] "gentlem[ae]n"%c within s;
RoyalSalutations = TAB "your"%c "royal"%c? "majesty|highness|excellence"%c within s;

DearSalutations = (?longest)(
    ([pos!="APPGE|AT1?" & word!=","] | <s>)
    [word="dear"%c] ([pos="NNB"] "\."?)?
    [pos="N.+|DB2?" & pos!="NN[UT][12]?" & word!="god|lord"%c]+
    ([pos="CC"] ([pos="NNB"] "\."?)? [pos="N.+|DB2?"]+)*
) within s;

/union[
    Salutations,
    CasualSalutations,
    GoodSalutations1,
    GoodSalutations2,
    GenericSalutations1,
    GenericSalutations2,
    RoyalSalutations,
    DearSalutations
];
```

#### Valedictions

**Query**:

1. unambiguous expressions (e.g., "best wishes")
2. ambiguous expressions with comma (e.g., "best,")

TODO: what about "X sends best wishes"
TODO: count coordinated expressions separately?

```cqp
Valedictions1 = (
    (<s> | [pos!="APPGE" & word!="your|their"]) [pos="IW"]?
    "personal|best|(warm|kind(est)?)"%c "regards|wishes"%c |
    "yours"%c "sincerely|faithfully|truly"%c |
    [pos="RG"]? "sincerely|truly|respectfully|cordially"%c "yours"%c
);

Valedictions2 = <s> "best|cheers|yours|cordially|respectfully|warmly|regards|sincerely|thanks"%c ",";
/union[Valedictions, Valedictions1, Valedictions2];
```

```cqp
/union[Greetings, Salutations, Valedictions];
/feature[Greetings];
```

### Adverbs

TODO: handle phrasal verbs (e.g., "throw away")

```cqp
define $SpaceWords < "wordlists/adverbs/SpaceWords.txt";
RLs = [: word!="look(s|ing|ed)?"%c :] [pos="RL(\d1)?" & word!="together|downstream" %c] within s;
SpaceWords = [pos="R[^P].+" & word=RE($SpaceWords)%c];

/union[SpaceAdverbs, RLs, SpaceWords];
/feature_count[SpaceAdverbs];

define $TimeWords < "wordlists/adverbs/TimeWords.txt";
RTs = [pos="RT(\d1)?"]; # only count ditto tags once
TimeWords = [pos="R[^P].+" & word=RE($TimeWords)%c];
TimeMetaphors = [word="look(s|ing|ed)?" %c] [word="forward|back(ward)?" %c] within s;
set TimeMetaphors match matchend;

/union[TimeAdverbs, RTs, TimeWords, TimeMetaphors];
/feature_count[TimeAdverbs];
```

## Themes

TODO: consider multiple themes?

### Textual

#### Continuatives

```cqp
InitialContinuatives = <s> [word="\p{P}"]? [pos="UH" | word="yes|no|well|oh|now|please"%c] | "no"%c [: word!="matter"%c :] within s;
/feature[InitialContinuatives];
```

#### Conjunctions

```cqp
define $ParatacticWords = "for and nor but or yet so either neither"; # fanboys plus (n)either
InitialCoordinators = <s> [word="\p{P}"]? [pos="CCB?" | word=RE($ParatacticWords)%c | (word="for"%c & pos="CS")] | [word="so"%c] [: pos!="JJ" :] within s;
InitialSubordinators = <s> [word="\p{P}"]? [pos="CS[ANTW]?" & word!="that"%c] within s;
/union[InitialConjunctions, InitialCoordinators, InitialSubordinators];
/feature[InitialConjunctions];
```

##### Conjunctive Adjuncts

Halliday & Matthiessen (2014: Table 3-4)

```cqp
InitialConjunctiveAdjuncts = <s> [word="\p{P}"]? /mwu_conjunctiveadjuncts[] within s;
/feature[InitialConjunctiveAdjuncts];
```

##### Ordinal Numbers

```cqp
InitialNumbers = <s> [word="\p{P}"]? [word="\d+"] [word="\p{P}"] within s;
/feature[InitialNumbers];
```

